**8. Error Handling**

```javascript
// Robust error handling
try {
    // Attempt to get required variables
    const baseUrl = pm.environment.get('baseUrl');
    if (!baseUrl) {
        throw new Error('baseUrl not configured in environment');
    }

    const apiKey = pm.environment.get('apiKey');
    if (!apiKey) {
        console.warn('apiKey not set, proceeding without authentication');
    }

    // Dynamic value generation
    const timestamp = Date.now();
    if (isNaN(timestamp)) {
        throw new Error('Failed to generate timestamp');
    }

    pm.variables.set('timestamp', timestamp);

} catch (error) {
    console.error('Pre-request script error:', error.message);
    // Set error flag for tests
    pm.variables.set('scriptError', true);
    pm.variables.set('errorMessage', error.message);
}
```

**9. Pre-request Script Best Practices**

```
✅ DO:
- Keep scripts focused and single-purpose
- Handle errors gracefully
- Log important steps for debugging
- Use async patterns when needed
- Clean up temporary variables
- Document complex logic
- Test scripts independently

❌ DON'T:
- Make scripts too long/complex
- Forget error handling
- Log sensitive data
- Create infinite loops
- Block main request for too long
- Ignore performance impact

Script Organization:
1. Variable validation
2. Authentication/token refresh
3. Data generation
4. Header preparation
5. Request modification
6. Logging
```
```

