- Test one thing per test (ideally)
- Use constants for expected values
- Handle both success and error cases
- Test edge cases
- Use schema validation for complex responses
- Log debugging information
- Save useful values to environment

❌ DON'T:
- Hardcode values that change
- Forget to test error responses
- Make tests dependent on each other
- Test too many things in one test
- Ignore performance
- Log sensitive data

Test Coverage Checklist:
□ Status codes (success & error)
□ Response time
□ Required headers
□ Response structure
□ Data types
□ Required fields
□ Business rules
□ Edge cases
□ Data relationships
□ Performance expectations
□ Security considerations
