```

**10. Script Optimization Checklist**

```
□ Use JSR223 with Groovy and caching enabled
□ Avoid Beanshell entirely
□ Use JSON/XML extractors instead of regex
□ Combine multiple extractions into one where possible
□ Use Variable Expression mode in If Controllers
□ Pre-calculate conditions in JSR223 when complex
□ Reuse objects in JSR223 scripts
□ Avoid creating objects in loops
□ Cache parser instances
□ Use primitive operations over collection methods when performance critical
□ Sample assertions rather than asserting every request
□ Use appropriate timer distribution for the behavior
□ Split large CSV files
□ Generate data on the fly when possible
□ Manage HTTP cache appropriately
□ Clear cookies for new sessions
□ Monitor script performance with profiling
```

**11. Script Performance Testing**

```groovy
// Add this to measure script performance
[ JSR223 PostProcessor: Measure Performance ]
Language: groovy
Script: |
    long start = System.nanoTime()

    // Your script logic here

    long duration = System.nanoTime() - start

    if (duration > 1_000_000) {  // > 1ms
        log.warn("Slow script execution: ${duration / 1_000_000}ms")

        // Store for analysis
        def slowScripts = props.get("slowScripts")
        if (slowScripts == null) slowScripts = []
        slowScripts << [
            thread: ctx.getThreadNum(),
            sampler: ctx.getCurrentSampler().getName(),
            duration: duration,
            time: System.currentTimeMillis()
        ]
        props.put("slowScripts", slowScripts)
    }

// Profile with JFR or VisualVM
// jcmd <pid> JFR.start name=JMeterProfile
// jcmd <pid> JFR.dump filename=profile.jfr
```

**12. Common Optimization Anti-Patterns**

```
❌ Using Beanshell for any logic
❌ Regular expressions on large JSON responses
❌ Multiple assertions doing the same validation
❌ Nested loops without calculating total iterations
❌ Creating new objects in JSR223 loops
❌ Using JavaScript in If Controllers
❌ Storing full response data during load tests
❌ Excessive logging
❌ Thread.sleep() in scripts
❌ Synchronized blocks in JSR223
❌ Large CSV files with All threads + Recycle
❌ Listeners enabled during load tests
❌ XML parsing with DOM (use XPath or streaming)
❌ Base64 encoding/decoding large data
❌ String concatenation in loops (use StringBuilder)
```

